// Math workout: one document exercising every compiler feature.
// It must compile with zero errors (check the final status line).
*doc_title(Math Workout)

# Variables and calc

<w> = 12
<h> = 5
<area> = calc(<w> * <h>)
A rectangle is <w> cm wide and <h> cm tall. Area: <w> . <h> = <area> cm².

<half> = 3,5
Double of <half> is calc(<half> * 2).
Thousands still work: calc(100,000 + 1).

# Fractions, roots, powers

*frac(2 ; 3)
*frac(x + 1 ; x - 1)
*pow(x ; 2)
*pow(x + 1 ; n)
*root(2 ; x)
*root(3 ; x + 1)
*cbrt(27)
*sqrt(16)
*abs(x - 5)

Nested: *frac(*sqrt(4) ; *pow(2 ; 3))

# Trigonometry and logarithms

*sin(x)
*cos(x)
*tan(x)
*cot(x)
*sec(x)
*csc(x)
*arcsin(x)
*arccos(x)
*arctan(x)
*sinh(x)
*cosh(x)
*tanh(x)
*coth(x)
*log(10)
*ln(2.718)

# Sums, products, limits

*sum(i = 1 ; n ; i)
*prod(i = 1 ; n ; i)
*lim(x -> 0 ; sin(x) / x)

# Integrals

*int(x^2)
*int(x^2 ; x)
*int(0 ; 1 ; x^2)
*int(0 ; 1 ; x^2 ; x)
*oint(C ; F ; l)
*integral(0 ; 1 ; x^2)

# Piecewise functions and equation systems

*cases(x + y = 3 | x - y = 1)

*cases(x ; x > 0 | 0 ; x <= 0)

*cases(
    x ; x > 0
    0 ; x <= 0
)

# Vectors and binomials

*vec(AB)
*binom(n ; k)
*binom(5 ; 2)

# Matrices and tables

*matrix(1 ; 2 | 3 ; 4)
*mat(a ; b | c ; d)

*table(Name ; Age | Alice ; 20 | Bob ; 22)

# Inline math and subscripts

The solution is \ x = 2 \.

Discriminant: \ b^2 - 4ac \

Corners A_1 and x_n, vector *vec(AB).

# Spacing and symbols

a *quad b *qquad c *thin d *med e

*alpha *beta *gamma *pi *infinity

If x >= 0 and x <= 10 then x != 5 => done.

# Plots

*plot(x^2 ; -5 ; 5)
*plot(sin(x) ; -10 ; 10)

# Everything combined

<k> = 3
*frac(*int(0 ; <k> ; x^2) ; *binom(calc(<k> + 1) ; 2))
